          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at 6 years of age. Seizures currently occur approximately once per week. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to a causative **STXBP1** variant, **c.902A>G**, and is drug-resistant.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Perampanel  \n- Oxcarbazepine  \n- Lamotrigine  \n- Lacosamide  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nApproximately one focal impaired-awareness seizure per week.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures, associated with the causative STXBP1 c.902A>G variant.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen and monitor seizure frequency. Continue epilepsy clinic follow-up.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
